      },
      "lineNbr": 161,
      "author": {
        "id": 1361259
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-11-24T22:54:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Figure 425 shows VCCST_PWRGD falling before VCCST itself (which may even remain powered), so that ordering doesn\u0027t seem to matter. \n\nMinimizing delay on VCCST_PG_OD seems better, to satistfy tCPU28a (keeping SLP_S3 assertion -\u003e VCCST_PWRGD under the 200 us max), and tCPU28b even appears to say that VCCST_PWRGD should fall before VCCST turns off.",
      "parentUuid": "3ae84fca_1ea3432a",
      "revId": "71519c104014477aed0eba04033cd80fe46c8e47",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
