      "writtenOn": "2019-11-22T02:26:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We need to look at CPU_C10_GATE_L before enabling S0 rails.\n\nAlso, we need to turn this on before enabling VCCIO. (per CML PDG note 14 page 640)\n\nLastly, we should make a separate function to handle C10_GATE_L changes as we can use that to turn off VCCSTG and VCCIO. (bold statement in pg. 598 of CML PDG).",
      "revId": "71519c104014477aed0eba04033cd80fe46c8e47",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "dc8fe2e4_ee4edecc",
        "filename": "power/cometlake-discrete.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 312,
      "author": {
        "id": 1361259
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-11-24T22:54:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There\u0027s a TODO further up to handle CPU_C10_GATE_L; the proto hardware should not do this gating because EN_S0_RAILS also controls power to the HDMI ports (in addition to PP1200_PLLOC and PP1050_STG) and we don\u0027t want to cut that power while still in S0. EC doesn\u0027t need to touch the VCCIO enable because CPU_C10_GATED_L is directly connected to the VCCIO regulator\u0027s LP_L input.\n\nMoved enable to before VCCIO.",
      "parentUuid": "1b2d0c65_9ebccd54",
      "revId": "71519c104014477aed0eba04033cd80fe46c8e47",
